# Copy to .kamal/secrets and fill in. NEVER commit the filled version —
# .kamal/secrets is gitignored on purpose.
#
# Kamal sources this file at deploy time and exposes each line as an
# environment variable to:
#   - the `password:` lookup under registry: (KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD)
#   - the `env: secret:` list under deploy.yml (CORP_API_KEY, …)
#
# Anything Kamal needs as a secret must be listed in deploy.yml's
# `env: secret:` AND defined here. Anything else is ignored.

# --- 1. Registry credentials ---
# Get this from your registry.axgrid.com admin UI (User → API tokens /
# Robot accounts). Use a token, not your personal login password —
# tokens can be rotated without locking your account out.
KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=replace-me

# --- 2. corp-ui per-service API key ---
# In the corp-ui admin console (https://ui.r.axgrid.com):
#   Admin → Services → discovery → Edit → "Regenerate API key"
# Copy the displayed `cks_…` value here. The key starts with `cks_`.
CORP_API_KEY=cks_replace-me

# --- 3. Discovery static admin tokens (optional but recommended) ---
# Comma-separated list of bearer tokens that bypass corp-ui auth and
# get RoleAdmin. Useful for emergency access if corp-ui is down, and
# for the discovery2-client library when it registers services from
# CI without a human in the loop. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Leave empty if you don't need an admin token (you can still use
# corp-ui SSO normally).
DISCOVERY_ADMIN_TOKENS=
